/P 122 0 R
/T (Relational: Excellent for complex queries. Joins, aggregation, GROUP BY and ad-hoc reporting are optimized by mature query planners and indexes. Performance can drop when a query joins many large tables, or when a single server becomes the write bottleneck.)
/E (Relational: Excellent for complex queries. Joins, aggregation, GROUP BY and ad-hoc reporting are optimized by mature query planners and indexes. Performance can drop when a query joins many large tables, or when a single server becomes the write bottleneck.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
170 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 122 0 R
/T (NoSQL: Excellent for simple access patterns at very high volume: read or write one key or one document in milliseconds. Data is usually denormalized so that everything needed for a request sits in one record and no join is needed. The trade-off is that queries not planned for at design time \(cross-collection reports, ad-hoc joins\) are slow or awkward.)
/E (NoSQL: Excellent for simple access patterns at very high volume: read or write one key or one document in milliseconds. Data is usually denormalized so that everything needed for a request sits in one record and no join is needed. The trade-off is that queries not planned for at design time \(cross-collection reports, ad-hoc joins\) are slow or awkward.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
