/T (Relational and NoSQL databases solve different problems. Relational databases give strong consistency, enforced relationships and rich querying, which is why the core of the Airline Reservation System \(bookings, seats, payments and tickets\) belongs in a relational design, and why constraints such as a unique seat per flight are needed to prevent the anomalies identified in the design analysis. NoSQL databases give effortless horizontal scaling, flexibility and speed, which makes them a strong choice for caching, logs, user activity and route analysis around that core.)
/E (Relational and NoSQL databases solve different problems. Relational databases give strong consistency, enforced relationships and rich querying, which is why the core of the Airline Reservation System \(bookings, seats, payments and tickets\) belongs in a relational design, and why constraints such as a unique seat per flight are needed to prevent the anomalies identified in the design analysis. NoSQL databases give effortless horizontal scaling, flexibility and speed, which makes them a strong choice for caching, logs, user activity and route analysis around that core.)
/Pg 17 0 R
