586 0 obj
<<
/Title (NoSQL: Excellent for simple access patterns at very high volume: read or write one key or one document in milliseconds. Data is usually denormalized so that everything needed for a request sits in one record and no join is needed. The trade-off is that queries not planned for at design time \(cross-collection reports, ad-hoc joins\) are slow or awkward.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 560 0 R
/Prev 585 0 R
>>
endobj
